---
// Marah OS: what it is, the three steps, and four cards about living with it.
---

<section
  class="border-y border-line py-24 [background:radial-gradient(ellipse_at_80%_10%,rgba(76,139,220,.2),transparent_55%),var(--color-night)] max-sm:py-16"
  id="os"
  aria-labelledby="os-title"
>
  <div class="wrap grid grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] items-center gap-18 max-md:grid-cols-1 max-md:gap-8">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Marah OS</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 mb-5 text-section" id="os-title">
        Turn a spare PC
        <br />
        <span class="accent-text">into a game console.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="my-[1em] max-w-[560px] text-lead text-muted">
        Marah OS is a small Linux system, built on Fedora with bootc. Marah Launcher is the whole screen: turn the PC on
        and your games are there, with no desktop and no password to type.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3.5">
        <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/MarahHQ/marah-os/releases/latest">
          Get the USB stick image
        </a>
        <a class="btn-outline" href="#needs">
          What my PC needs <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[560px] text-lead text-muted" data-release="os">
        The latest release
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-[560px] rounded-[18px] border border-line bg-panel p-5" id="check-iso">
        <h3 class="text-lead">Check the download</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-small text-muted">
          Join the parts first. Keep the ISO's <code>.sha256</code> file beside the ISO, then run the command for your
          system. Linux and macOS print <code>OK</code> when the ISO is whole.
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-small">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[72px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 max-sm:grid-cols-1 max-sm:gap-0.5">
            <dt class="font-bold">Linux</dt>
            <dd class="sum-cmd">
              <code>
                sha256sum -c <span data-os-file="sum">marah-os-x86_64-*.iso.sha256</span>
              </code>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[72px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 max-sm:grid-cols-1 max-sm:gap-0.5">
            <dt class="font-bold">macOS</dt>
            <dd class="sum-cmd">
              <code>
                shasum -a 256 -c <span data-os-file="sum">marah-os-x86_64-*.iso.sha256</span>
              </code>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[72px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-3 max-sm:grid-cols-1 max-sm:gap-0.5">
            <dt class="font-bold">Windows</dt>
            <dd class="sum-cmd">
              <code>
                certutil -hashfile <span data-os-file="iso">marah-os-x86_64-&lt;version&gt;.iso</span> SHA256
              </code>
              <span class="block text-muted">
                Then compare the hash with the one in the <code>.sha256</code> file.
              </span>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-1.5" data-os-sums hidden>
          <p class="text-small text-muted">Each part's SHA-256, as GitHub has it:</p>
          <ul class="grid gap-1.5"></ul>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-small text-muted">
          The ISO's SHA-256 file:
          <a data-os-sum-link href="https://github.com/MarahHQ/marah-os/releases/latest">
            on the latest release
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps grid gap-4" data-stagger>
      <li>
        <strong class="block text-lead">Put it on a USB stick.</strong>
        <span class="text-body text-muted">
          Any stick of 4&nbsp;GB or more. The release has the image, sometimes in parts: download every part and join
          them, as <a href="https://github.com/MarahHQ/marah-os#readme">the README shows</a>. Then write the ISO to the
          stick with <a href="https://etcher.balena.io/">balenaEtcher</a> or
          <a href="https://github.com/FedoraQt/MediaWriter">Fedora Media Writer</a>.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="block text-lead">Start the PC from the stick.</strong>
        <span class="text-body text-muted">
          Press the boot menu key as the PC starts (often F12, F11, F8 or Esc) and pick the stick. Marah OS runs from
          it. Nothing on the PC changes.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="block text-lead">Try it, or install it.</strong>
        <span class="text-body text-muted">
          Play from the stick first if you like. To install, pick a disk of 40&nbsp;GB or more and wait a few minutes.
          From then on the PC starts straight into your games.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap mt-16 grid grid-cols-4 gap-4.5 max-lg:grid-cols-2 max-sm:grid-cols-1" data-stagger>
    <article class="rounded-[20px] border border-line bg-panel p-6">
      <h3 class="mb-2.5 text-[19px]">Everything from the sofa</h3>
      <p class="mb-3.5 text-body text-muted">
        Internet, Sound and Bluetooth are in Settings → System, with the system's updates. You set them up with the
        controller.
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px]">
          <span>Internet</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">Connected</em>
        </li>
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px]">
          <span>Sound</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">TV (HDMI)</em>
        </li>
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px]">
          <span>Bluetooth</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">Controller</em>
        </li>
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px]">
          <span>Marah OS updates</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">Up to date</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-[20px] border border-line bg-panel p-6">
      <h3 class="mb-2.5 text-[19px]">Updates you never have to fear</h3>
      <p class="mb-3.5 text-body text-muted">
        The system and Marah Launcher update together, as one image, in the background. An update waits for the next
        start, so it never stops a game. If an update breaks something, the version before it is still in the boot menu:
        hold Shift or Esc as the PC starts and pick it.
      </p>
      <ul class="grid gap-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px] outline-2 outline-ice">
          <span>Marah OS</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">the newest</em>
        </li>
        <li class="flex justify-between gap-3 rounded-[10px] bg-deep px-3 py-[9px] text-[13.5px]">
          <span>Marah OS</span>
          <em class="text-muted not-italic">the one before</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-[20px] border border-line bg-panel p-6" id="needs">
      <h3 class="mb-2.5 text-[19px]">What your PC needs</h3>
      <dl class="grid gap-2.5">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-small font-bold">Processor</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-small leading-[1.45] text-muted">64-bit (x86-64). PS4 games need AVX2.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-small font-bold">Graphics</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-small leading-[1.45] text-muted">
            Vulkan 1.3, for PS4 and PS5 games. NVIDIA's driver is set up by itself.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-small font-bold">To play well</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-small leading-[1.45] text-muted">
            PS4: 8 threads, 8&nbsp;GB of memory, a 4&nbsp;GB graphics card. PS5: 12 threads, 16&nbsp;GB, an 8&nbsp;GB
            card.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-small font-bold">Disk</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 text-small leading-[1.45] text-muted">
            40&nbsp;GB or more, and internet for games and updates.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-3 text-caption text-muted">
        Marah Launcher checks your PC too: Settings → This PC says how each console's games should run.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-[20px] border border-line bg-panel p-6">
      <h3 class="mb-2.5 text-[19px]">Keep what you have</h3>
      <p class="mb-3.5 text-body text-muted">
        Installing on a whole disk erases it, so keep your games on another one. To keep another system, or to use free
        space, pick <strong>Choose partitions instead</strong>: Fedora's installer does the rest.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
